exercises.solution:
```python
def greeting(name, language="en"):
    if language == "es":
        return f"¡Hola, {name}!"
    elif language == "sw":
        return f"Habari, {name}!"
    return f"Hello, {name}!"
```

The default `"en"` is used whenever the caller leaves `language` out. Putting the English case last makes it the fallback for every code not listed. Each `return` ends the call, so no `else` is needed.

